A||||8||Ken Wittlief||How loud should the fuel pump be?||||5||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||01:55 PM||||since my car is not running super rich anymore it has quieted down somewhat, and I have noticed when driving with all the windows and sunroof closed (which is not very often) - i noticed I hear the fuel pump running all the time.<P>  Its a cross between a hum and a buzz - I do have my radio pulled out right now for repairs and the sound seems to be mostly comeing from that area.<P>   Is the fuel pump suppose to be loud enough to hear it with when the engine is running? Or is this a bad sign?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||05-24-2001||02:03 PM||||For what it's worth, the pump on my 84 has been loud enough to hear inside the car ever since it was new.  Even after replacing it about 6 years ago it's still noisy.  On the other hand, the pump in my 88 is very quiet.  I wouldn't be too concerned unless the noise changes or gets significantly louder.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||05-24-2001||02:04 PM||||I can usually hear mine when i turn the key to on before i start it up, but i don't usually notice it while driving, although it does seem loud enough that i'm sure i could hear it if i looked for it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||05-24-2001||02:16 PM||||I can hear mine for a couple seconds when I first turn on the key.  I had one a couople years ago that was noisey and eventually it made my gas gauge freak out and read full when full and a 1/4 of a tank from then on until it got less then a 1/4. Then it would read normal until emtpy.  I found out it was an aftermarket pump.  I made it through two tanks of gas before I could get it fixed up in Sacramento at a dealership where a friend is service manager.(boy does that help to get good service.)cost? About 300.00 P&L||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||02:18 PM||||Thanks guys - I guess Im spoiled by my 2000 Saturn SL - at 75 mph the loudest thing you hear is the wind across the radio antenna outside (pulled it off once to confirm thats what it was)<P>  and at idle speed at a red light you usually hear the other cars around you - like the saturn had stalled.<P>  My fiero has exhaust noise at idle - i dont expect it to ever be silent, but the drone of the fuel pump - now a days in a new car - that would be unacceptable - if you can hear it at all it would be too loud.<P>   Thanks for the replies - I wont worry about it unless it stops (c:||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-24-2001||08:07 PM||||only time i notice mine is when im getting low on gas. I like the warning. I try to keep at least a 1/4 all the time<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||PBJ||05-24-2001||08:48 PM||||Mine is noisy, too when I am really low on gas and it starts sucking air, about 2 or 3 kms before I am walking with the gas can in hand.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||05-24-2001||11:23 PM||||I have been driving with my dash and center console out for about a week and have noticed the fuel pump was pretty noisy. I hear it all the time, it changes at I accel and slow down beacuse the shifting gas in the tank, but I hear it when Im driving and sitting still. It brand new also, and fairly noisy. I don't notice it with the console on though.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||05-25-2001||10:18 AM||||Mine's been loud ever since I got the car (about 6 months ago).  The dealership says that it's about to go when it gets loud, but I'm not going to worry about it until I have to walk.  At $150 for the job, I'd rather keep that money in the bank a little longer (drawning interest).<P>MM||||reg||1
